    "instruction": "Diagnostic condition: you may edit ONLY the BODY of the named focus function. Keep its signature, all other functions, their order, and every other body unchanged. Do not add/delete functions. Infer the best valid local implementation from the examples. If that boundary cannot solve the task, preserve the best valid program and state the limitation in scope/change.",
    "current_program": "def visible_rows(actions):\n    rows = []\n    saved = []\n    for action in actions:\n        op = action[\"op\"]\n        if op == \"put\":\n            rows.append(action[\"id\"])\n        elif op == \"delete\":\n            if action[\"id\"] in rows:\n                rows.remove(action[\"id\"])\n        elif op == \"begin\":\n            saved = list(rows)\n        elif op == \"rollback\":\n            rows = list(saved)\n    return sorted(rows)\n\ndef next_id(rows):\n    return max(rows + [0]) + 1\n\ndef investigate(context, acquire):\n    return next_id(visible_rows(context[\"actions\"]))\n",
